[N 22-23 Redridge]
[D Forever Shaman 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Second Redridge pass: the Goldshire and Tower of Azora errands on the walk in, Lakeshire's leftovers, the north loop with the Keeshan escort, the long south and east loop (Old Lion Statue chain, Stonewatch Keep elites, the Red Waterskin) and the hearth to Westfall.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffRedridge 22-23|r  -  you start at Sentinel Hill at level ~22 with the hearth still set there (do not rebind it in Lakeshire). About 21,600 quest XP from 15 turn-ins, nearly all of it in two loops out of Lakeshire. |cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r parts: Shadow Magic and Tharil'zun at Stonewatch Keep and the Keeshan escort, 7,400 XP between them.
[OC]|cffffcc00Open when you leave:|r Messenger to Westfall (144, chapter 16), Morganth (249, the elite is killed in chapter 16), What Comes Around... (386, the Stockade is chapter 15) and, shaman, the filled Red Waterskin (94499, hand in to Hervdana in the Wetlands).

[OC]|cffffffffStormwind and the road east|r
At [TAR523 Thor], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Stormwind]|r [G56.5,52.6 Westfall]
[O][A Hunter] At [TAR5515 Einris Brightspear] in the Dwarven District, [T] train your level 22 spells [G67.3,36.3 Stormwind City]
[O][A Hunter] Next door at [TAR5510 Thulman Flintcrag], buy 600 Heavy Shot for the long loops below [G62.0,36.6 Stormwind City]
[O][A Shaman] There is no shaman trainer in Stormwind: if you are 22 and want the rank-ups now, take the tram to Ironforge (otherwise they wait for chapter 11) [G73.8,49.2 Stormwind City]
[O][A Shaman] In the Forlorn Cavern at [TAR258098 Eldrun Stormbreaker], [T] train your level 22 spells [G47.1,13.8 Ironforge]
[O][A Shaman] Tram back to Stormwind [G76.5,51.5 Ironforge]
[OC]Take the road out of the gate to Goldshire, then on to the Tower of Azora and the Redridge border. Two quest stops on the way
At [TAR514 Smith Argus] at the Goldshire blacksmith, [QT118] [QA119 Return to Verner] (the Crate of Horseshoes goes back to Verner in Lakeshire) [G41.7,65.5 Elwynn Forest]
At [TAR2329 Michelle Belle] in the Lion's Pride Inn, learn Wool Bandage (First Aid 80, 1 Wool Cloth each) and Journeyman First Aid if you still lack it [G43.4,65.6 Elwynn Forest]
At the Tower of Azora at [TAR313 Theocritus], [QA94 A Watchful Eye] (take the Glyph of Azora to the Old Lion Statue in eastern Redridge - chapter 16 hands Morganth in here) [G65.2,69.7 Elwynn Forest]
Run east along the road into Redridge: Three Corners [G10.2,72.0 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cffffcc00Merchant camp|r is right here (10,72): sell, hand in any Waylaid Supplies to [TAR256389 Tamelyn Aldridge] (10.4,71.4), and only if you already have 4+ Pristine Leather and are switching to Leatherworking, buy the Totemic (shaman) / Brawler's (hunter) patterns from [TAR256734 Daniel Stitchsong] (10,72.4) - details in chapter 06
[OC]Follow the road northeast from Three Corners to Lakeshire (~2 minutes) - it is the same road as chapter 06

[OC]|cffffffffLakeshire|r  -  pick everything up first; the loops below come back here
At the stables at [TAR415 Verner Osgood], [QT119] [QA122 Underbelly Scales] [QA124 A Baying of Gnolls] [G25.9,47.3 Redridge Mountains]
At [TAR341 Foreman Oslow], [QA98386 Alther's Mill] (12 Greater Tarantulas + 6 eggs at the mill east of the lake, 1,650 XP) [G27.1,48.6 Redridge Mountains]
At [TAR381 Dockmaster Baren] on the dock, [QA150 Murloc Poachers] (8 Murloc Fins from the lake murlocs) [G22.6,47.4 Redridge Mountains]
In the town hall at [TAR900 Bailiff Conacher], [QA91 Solomon's Law] (10 Shadowhide Pendants from the gnolls around the Tower of Ilgalar) [G24.6,44.3 Redridge Mountains]
Next door at [TAR344 Magistrate Solomon], [QT121] [QA143 Messenger to Westfall] (you hand this in at Sentinel Hill when you hearth home) [G24.9,44.5 Redridge Mountains]
[O][A Hunter] Across the bridge at [TAR3088 Henry Chapal], top up Heavy Shot before the loops [G18.8,41.3 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cffffcc00Order:|r north first (Brutes, Verner, Yowler, Keeshan - the easy loop apart from the escort camp), then the long south and east arc. |cff66ff66normal|r below means it finishes in one pass of that loop; the two |cffffcc00slow|r items are named where they come up

[OC]|cffffffffLoop 1: the gnoll hills and Keeshan|r
Kill 10 [TAR426 Redridge Brute] and 8 [TAR430 Redridge Mystic] in the hills north of Lakeshire - |cff66ff66normal|r (level 17-19, 44 spawns between them, they come in pairs) [QC124] [G18.9,37.3 Redridge Mountains]
At [TAR415 Verner Osgood], [QT124] [QA126 Howling in the Hills] [G25.9,47.3 Redridge Mountains]
Run north to the gnoll camp and kill [TAR518 Yowler] (level 25, not elite) for Yowler's Paw - |cff66ff66normal|r, one named gnoll [QC126] [G22.6,21.4 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+ escort|r  -  everyone in the group must be on the quest before you talk to the NPC. Corporal Keeshan is a level 25 elite held in a cave in the Blackrock camp just north of Yowler (cave: Classic-era description, unverified on Forever); the camp is Champions (24-25), Trackers (23-24) and Summoners (22-23), plus four elite Shadowcasters at its east edge (30.5,8). Clear the approach to the cave first, then accept and walk him home down the road to Lakeshire
|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r At [TAR349 Corporal Keeshan] in the Blackrock camp, [QA219 Missing In Action] [G23.3,12.6 Redridge Mountains]
|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r Escort Keeshan south to Lakeshire and stay beside him all the way [QC219] [G28.4,49.0 Redridge Mountains]
At [TAR382 Marshal Marris], [QT219] [G28.4,49.0 Redridge Mountains]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear:|r Bone-studded Leather (leather chest, 86 armor, +6 Str +1 Agi +5 Sta) unless your chest is already better. Robe of Solomon is cloth and Deputy Chain Coat is mail - pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear:|r Bone-studded Leather only if your chest is below 86 armor - its +6 Str does nothing for a hunter. Robe of Solomon is cloth and Deputy Chain Coat is mail - pass
At the stables at [TAR415 Verner Osgood], [QT126] [G25.9,47.3 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear:|r Ring of Iron Will (+4 Sta +2 Spi) for both of you; Gold Militia Boots are mail - pass

[OC]|cffffffffLoop 2: south hills, east shore, Stonewatch and the Tower of Ilgalar|r  -  one long arc, the Mill on the way out and the gnolls last
Cross the bridge and kill Black Dragon Whelps on the south hills for 6 Underbelly Whelp Scales - |cff66ff66normal|r (level 17-18, 34 spawns across the south of the zone) [QC122] [G31.9,63.0 Redridge Mountains]
Work east along the south shore and kill [TAR422 Murloc Flesheater] and [TAR548 Murloc Minor Tidecaller] for 8 Murloc Fins - |cff66ff66normal|r but a ~31% drop: budget ~30 murlocs, then let it go (the whole south and east shore is murlocs, ~100 spawns; the Tidecallers at 51.8,52.8 and the Nightcrawlers at the falls drop them too) [QC150] [G50.8,60.1 Redridge Mountains]
Up the east shore to Alther's Mill: kill 12 [TAR271898 Greater Tarantula] and destroy the 6 Tarantula Eggs among them (no egg coordinates in the DB) - |cff66ff66normal|r (level 18-19, 75 spawns around the mill) [QC98386] [G46.4,41.3 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cffffffffEast|r  -  from x 64 the road runs through Shadowhide gnolls: Gnolls 22-23 on the west side (x 64-72), Brutes 23-24 on the north slope (73.5,41), Slayers and Darkweavers 25-26, Warriors 24-25 and the Servants of Ilgalar (24-25) around the tower. Kill what blocks the road now, the pendants come last. |cFFFF0000Stonewatch Keep|r (x 60-66, y 52-60) is a fort of elites: 31 Sentries (21-22), 30 Shadowcasters (22-23), 16 Hunters (23-24), 5 Gladiators (24-25), Singe (24) and Gath'Ilzogg (26, chapter 16's target) - never walk into the keep itself
Take the road east to the Old Lion Statue and hand in the Glyph [QT94] [QA248 Looking Further] [G79.4,46.8 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cFFFF0000Morganth|r (level 26 elite) stands in the Tower of Ilgalar about 5 map units west of the statue (75.0,49.5), with his gnolls and Servants around him. Do not pull him now - chapter 16 kills him with a group. HP is not in the Forever DB for any of the elites here
[A Shaman] Walk south to the foot of Stonewatch Falls beside the Murloc Nightcrawlers (level 21-22) and use the Unfilled Red Waterskin there [QC94499] [G76.1,59.6 Redridge Mountains]
[OC][A Shaman] The DB has no object for the falls; the quest text puts it near the Nightcrawlers, whose only spawns are here (76.1,59.6). Rohh the Silent (a level 26 rare) also has spawn points in this corner - leave him. Keep the filled skin: Hervdana takes it in the Wetlands
|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r Stonewatch Keep, south end: kill [TAR486 Tharil'zun] (level 24 elite) and loot his head [QC19] [G64.4,59.4 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]Singe (24 elite) and Gath'Ilzogg (26 elite) stand 3-4 map units north of Tharil'zun and a Gladiator (24-25 elite) with them: pull Tharil'zun south, away from them, before you fight, or the whole south end joins in
|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r Kill [TAR436 Blackrock Shadowcaster] for 3 Midnight Orbs - pull the ones on the keep's west edge one at a time [QC115] [G60.4,54.8 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cffffcc00Label - slow:|r the orbs are the slowest item of the chapter: elite casters, drop chance not in the DB, so give it a fair few pulls and no more. There is also a lone Shadowcaster at the tower's foot (58.4,49.4) and four at the north camp by Keeshan. If it stalls the quest can stay in the log - chapter 16 passes Lakeshire again
Climb the intact watch tower beside the keep and click An Empty Jar to hand in the Glyph [QT248] [G58.2,49.8 Redridge Mountains]
Walk back east to the statue and take Morganth (the fight itself is chapter 16) [QA249 Morganth] [G79.4,46.8 Redridge Mountains]
Kill [TAR433 Shadowhide Gnoll] for 10 Shadowhide Pendants [QC91] [G69.2,49.2 Redridge Mountains]
[OC]|cffffcc00Label - slow:|r the DB lists four pendant droppers (Gnoll, Brute, Slayer, Darkweaver - not the Warriors) but no drop chance. Stay on the 22-24 gnolls (Gnolls on the west side, Brutes on the north slope at 73.9,41.0) and take the 25-26 Slayers and Darkweavers one at a time near the tower. Item-start side quest: if a Glowing Shadowhide Pendant drops (Darkweavers and Slayers, per the digest), right-click it for Theocritus' Retrieval, 1,400 XP for Theocritus - chapter 16 passes the Tower of Azora but does not list it
[OC]Run back west along the road to Lakeshire (~3 minutes)

